meta {
  name: Set summon rewards
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/summons
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "enabled": true,
    "pointsPerSummon": 5,
    "dailyPointCap": 100,
    "pairCooldownMinutes": 30,
    "announceEvery": 50
  }
}

tests {
  test("saves the settings", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getBody().rewards.pointsPerSummon).to.equal(5);
  });
}

docs {
  What a summon is worth, and the rules that stop it being farmed. Fields left
  out keep their current value.

  - `pointsPerSummon` — 0 counts summons without paying for them.
  - `dailyPointCap` — most points one account can earn from summons in 24h;
    0 removes the cap. Must be at least `pointsPerSummon`.
  - `pairCooldownMinutes` — how long before the same two accounts pay each
    other again; 0 always pays.
  - `announceEvery` — announce every Nth realm summon in game; 0 stays quiet.

  Summoning an alt on your own account never pays, and that is not tunable.
  Turning `enabled` off keeps the counter running: those summons are recorded
  as unpaid and are never paid retroactively when you turn it back on.

  This body is the shipped default, so running the collection leaves the realm
  as it was.
}
